{{Trail|Linguistics}}
The '''Dragon Alphabet''' is the alphabet used for the [[Lore:Dragon Language|Dragon Language]]. Text  written in the Dragon Alphabet is found on walls in ancient dungeons and on burial grounds in the form of [[Lore:Word Walls|Word Walls]].{{Ref|name=DLMNM|{{Cite Book|Dragon Language: Myth no More}}}} The alphabet consists of 34 symbols: 25 that map directly to letters in the Latin alphabet, and nine that represent pairs of letters. There is a symbol for every letter in the Latin alphabet.

The shape of the letters is constrained by their need to be written using three large talons and a vestigial fourth digit called the dewclaw. Thus, all of the character symbols consist of a maximum of three scratches occasionally punctuated with a dot from the dewclaw.{{ref|name=SDS|group=UOL|[http://www.gameinformer.com/b/features/archive/2011/01/20/skyrim-s-dragon-shouts.aspx?PostPageIndex&#61;3 Skyrim's Dragon Shouts], GameInformer, January 20, 2011}}

